\f2\fs40\par
Concerning the Service\i0\fs22\par
\par
\par
\fs20 The death of a member of the Church should be reported as soon as\par
possible to, and arrangements for the funeral should be made in\par
consultation with, the Minister of the Congregation.\par
 \par
Baptized Christians are properly buried from the church. The service\par
should be held at a time when the congregation has opportunity to be\par
present.\par
 \par
The coffin is to be closed before the service, and it remains closed\par
thereafter. It is appropriate that it be covered with a pall or other\par
suitable covering.\par
 \par
If necessary, or if desired, all or part of the service of Committal\par
may be said in the church.  If preferred, the Committal service may take\par
place before the service in the church. It may also be used prior to\par
cremation.\par
 \par
A priest normally presides at the service.  It is appropriate that the\par
bishop, when present, preside at the Eucharist and pronounce the\par
Commendation.\par
 \par
It is desirable that the Lesson from the Old Testament, and the\par
Epistle, be read by lay persons.\par
 \par
When the services of a priest cannot be obtained, a deacon or lay\par
reader may preside at the service.\par
 \par
At the burial of a child, the passages from Lamentations, 1 John, and\par
John 6, together with Psalm 23, are recommended.\par
 \par
It is customary that the celebrant meet the body and go before it into\par
the church or towards the grave.\par
 \par
The anthems at the beginning of the service are sung or said as the\par
body is borne into the church, or during the entrance of the ministers,\par
or by the celebrant standing in the accustomed place.\par
 \par
\par
\fs48 The Burial of the Dead:\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Rite Two\fs20\par
 \par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\i All stand while one or more of the following anthems are sung or said. A\par
hymn, psalm, or some other suitable anthem may be sung instead\i0 .\par
 \par
\fs24 I am Resurrection and I am Life, says the Lord.\par
Whoever has faith in me shall have life,\par
even though he die.\par
And everyone who has life,\par
and has committed himself to me in faith,\par
shall not die for ever.\par
 \par
As for me, I know that my Redeemer lives\par
and that at the last he will stand upon the earth.\par
After my awaking, he will raise me up;\par
and in my body I shall see God.\par
I myself shall see, and my eyes behold him\par
who is my friend and not a stranger.\par
 \par
For none of us has life in himself,\par
and none becomes his own master when he dies.\par
For if we have life, we are alive in the Lord,\par
and if we die, we die in the Lord.\par
So, then, whether we live or die,\par
we are the Lord's possession.\par
\par
Happy from now on\par
are those who die in the Lord!\par
So it is, says the Spirit,\par
for they rest from their labors.\par
 \par
\i\fs20 Or else this anthem\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard In the midst of life we are in death;\par
from whom can we seek help?\par
From you alone, O Lord,\par
who by our sins are justly angered.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard  \i Holy God, Holy and Mighty,\par
Holy and merciful Savior,\par
deliver us not into the bitterness of eternal death\i0 .\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Lord, you know the secrets of our hearts;\par
shut not your ears to our prayers,\par
but spare us, O Lord.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i Holy God, Holy and Mighty,\par
Holy and merciful Savior,\par
deliver us not into the bitterness of eternal death\i0 .\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O worthy and eternal Judge,\par
do not let the pains of death\par
turn us away from you at our last hour.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i Holy God, Holy and Mighty,\par
Holy and merciful Savior,\par
deliver us not into the bitterness of eternal death\i0 .\par
