 \par
\b The Consecration of a Grave\b0\par
 \par
\i\fs20 If the grave is in a place that has not previously been set apart for\par
Christian burial, the Priest may use the following prayer, either before\par
the service of Committal or at some other convenient time\i0 .\fs24\par
 \par
O God, whose blessed Son was laid in a sepulcher in the\par
garden: Bless, we pray, this grave, and grant that \i he\i0  whose\par
body is (is to be) buried here may dwell with Christ in\par
paradise, and may come to your heavenly kingdom; through\par
your Son Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
 \par
\b Additional Prayers\b0\par
 \par
Almighty God, with whom still live the spirits of those who\par
die in the Lord, and with whom the souls of the faithful are in\par
joy and felicity: We give you heartfelt thanks for the good\par
examples of all your servants, who, having finished their\par
course in faith, now find rest and refreshment. May we, with\par
all who have died in the true faith of your holy Name, have\par
perfect fulfillment and bliss in your eternal and everlasting\par
glory; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\par
O God, whose days are without end, and whose mercies\par
cannot be numbered: Make us, we pray, deeply aware of the\par
shortness and uncertainty of human life; and let your Holy\par
Spirit lead us in holiness and righteousness all our days; that,\par
when we shall have served you in our generation, we may be\par
gathered to our ancestors, having the testimony of a good\par
conscience, in the communion of the Catholic Church, in the\par
confidence of a certain faith, in the comfort of a religious and\par
holy hope, in favor with you, our God, and in perfect charity\par
with the world.  All this we ask through Jesus Christ\par
our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
O God, the King of saints, we praise and glorify your holy\par
Name for all your servants who have finished their course in\par
your faith and fear: for the blessed Virgin Mary; for the holy\par
patriarchs, prophets, apostles, and martyrs; and for all your\par
other righteous servants, known to us and unknown; and we\par
pray that, encouraged by their examples, aided by their\par
prayers, and strengthened by their fellowship, we also may\par
be partakers of the inheritance of the saints in light; through\par
the merits of your Son Jesus Christ our Lord. \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
Lord Jesus Christ, by your death you took away the sting of\par
death:  Grant to us your servants so to follow in faith where\par
you have led the way, that we may at length fall asleep\par
peacefully in you and wake up in your likeness; for your\par
tender mercies\rquote  sake.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
Father of all, we pray to you for those we love, but see no\par
longer: Grant them your peace; let light perpetual shine upon\par
them; and, in your loving wisdom and almighty power, work\par
in them the good purpose of your perfect will; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord.  \i Amen\i0 .\par
 \par
\par
Merciful God, Father of our Lord Jesus Christ who is the\par
Resurrection and the Life: Raise us, we humbly pray, from\par
the death of sin to the life of righteousness; that when we\par
depart this life we may rest in him, and at the resurrection\par
receive that blessing which your well-beloved Son shall then\par
pronounce: "Come, you blessed of my Father, receive the\par
kingdom prepared for you from the beginning of the world."\par
Grant this, O merciful Father, through Jesus Christ, our\par
Mediator and Redeemer.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
Grant, O Lord, to all who are bereaved the spirit of faith and\par
courage, that they may have strength to meet the days to\par
come with steadfastness and patience; not sorrowing as those\par
without hope, but in thankful remembrance of your great\par
goodness, and in the joyful expectation of eternal life with\par
those they love.  And this we ask in the Name of Jesus Christ\par
our Savior.  \i Amen\i0 .\par
 \par
Almighty God, Father of mercies and giver of comfort: Deal\par
graciously, we pray, with all who mourn; that, casting all\par
their care on you, they may know the consolation of your\par
love; through Jesus Christ our Lord. \i Amen.\i0\par
