\fs48 An Order for Burial\fs24\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\i\fs20 When, for pastoral consideration, neither of the burial rites in this Book\par
is deemed appropriate, the following form is used.\i0\fs24\par
\fs20\par
1.   The body is received.  The celebrant may meet the body and conduct it \par
into the church or chapel, or it may be in place before the congregation assembles.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720  \par
\pard\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 2.   Anthems from Holy Scripture or psalms may be sung or said, or a\par
hymn may be sung.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720  \par
\pard\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 3.   Prayer may be offered for the bereaved.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720  \par
\pard\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 4.   One or more passages of Holy Scripture are read.  Psalms, hymns, or \par
anthems may follow the readings.  If there is to be a Communion, the last Reading is from the Gospel.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720  \par
\pard\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 5.   A homily may follow the Readings, and the Apostles' Creed may be\par
recited.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720  \par
\pard\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 6.   Prayer, including the Lord's Prayer, is offered for the deceased, for \par
those who mourn, and for the Christian community, remembering the\par
promises of God in Christ about eternal life.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720  \par
\pard\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 7.   The deceased is commended to God, and the body is committed to its\par
resting place. The committal may take place either where the preceding\par
service has been held, or at the graveside.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720  \par
\pard\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 8.   If there is a Communion, it precedes the commendation, and begins\par
with the Peace and Offertory of the Eucharist. Any of the authorized\par
eucharistic prayers may be used.\par
\b\par
Note:\b0\par
 \par
\i The liturgy for the dead is an Easter liturgy. It finds all its meaning in the resurrection. Because Jesus was raised from the dead, we too, shall be raised.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720  \par
\pard\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 The liturgy, therefore, is characterized by joy, in the certainty that\par
\ldblquote neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor principalities, nor things present, nor things to come, nor powers, nor height, nor depth, nor anything else \par
in all creation, will be able to separate us from the love of God in Christ Jesus our Lord.\rdblquote\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720  \par
\pard\tx0\tx1080\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3330\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 This joy, however, does not make human grief unchristian. The very love we have for each other in Christ brings deep sorrow when we are parted \par
by death. Jesus himself wept at the grave of his friend. So, while we \par
rejoice that one we love has entered into the nearer presence of our Lord, \par
we sorrow in sympathy with those who mourn.\i0\f4\par
